comments[5]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-11-03T05:56:40.892Z",pi-fleet-sdk-sentinel-1103,"npm test fails 5/567 on the pm-toolchain Dependabot branch. All five failures originate from the shared ambient receiver fixture's positive control asserting implicit.item.parent === focus after client.create({ title, createMode: 'progressive' }) without inheritFocus. pm-cli GH-1577 (2026.10.26) made focus inheritance explicit for SDK create. Expected fix: pass inheritFocus: true in that positive control create (or assert the new explicit behavior); then confirm the remaining exact-document assertions still hold. Also re-check the transfer/reconcile/import tests that rely on the same fixture."
  "2026-11-03T09:07:04.940Z",codex-toolchain-1103,"Reproduced all five failures in test/ambient-defaults.test.ts: every failure occurs in the positive control before importer execution. Root cause is pm-cli 2026.10.26 GH-1577, present in the actual PR pin 2026.10.28: SDK create now requires inheritFocus:true. Classification: test contract drift. Keep exact full-document assertions; opt the focused control in and add a default-create control proving no inherited parent. Production sourceCreateOptions already explicitly unsets missing parent, so no production change is required."
  "2026-11-03T09:36:44.809Z",codex-toolchain-1103,"Additional full-suite failure reproduced in isolation: the migration peer fixture waits for a freshly spawned process to import the entire SDK from inside the bounded beforeMutation guard. Under host contention this hits extension_mutation_guard_timed_out; the guard remains correct. Classification: test synchronization bug. Preload the independent peer before migration, then release it with an explicit pipe signal at the same listed/located/read/schema/update/locked boundary. Keep every exact peer document, revision, history and receipt assertion; preserve the native guard deadline and ensure child cleanup/rejections are observed."
  "2026-11-03T09:52:33.570Z",codex-toolchain-1103,"Final focused validation: node --test test/ambient-defaults.test.ts passes 6/6, including every exact full document, and node --test test/identity-migration.test.ts passes 8/8 after peer prewarming. Focused peer boundary test also passes through pm test (117638ms). Typecheck, build:test and docstring pass; npm test ran build/build:test and the broad suite, found the old peer bootstrap timeout, and was interrupted after roughly 44 minutes while large unchanged property tests remained active. It is not a completed full-suite pass. Both changed test files are now independently verified. Changelog regenerated and checked with fetched tags, with no content diff; dist is not tracked. No production change, release gate, or coverage run was needed."
  "2026-11-03T09:55:34.409Z",codex-toolchain-1103,"Interrupted broad-run receipt: 508 reported tests, 499 pass, 3 fail, 6 canceled, no skips. Besides the corrected peer-bootstrap guard timeout, the other reported failures are a sidecar-adversarial fuzz subprocess ETIMEDOUT and the transfer coordinator test reaching its 120000ms deadline. Large outgoing/transfer properties and queued files were canceled when the already-failing run was stopped. These are explicit remaining local timing/coverage gaps; no complete full-suite pass is claimed. Current ambient defaults 6/6 and identity migration 8/8 both pass, and the current peer boundary passes via pm test."
